      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I also want to add that I agree that vagueness in the descriptions of shop items is a very frustrating trend. This was a big problem with the pets sold during last Spookality.\n\nAlmost everybody I ran into that bought a Treats pet was completely oblivious to the fact that the wings were randomized and not customizable until they had already purchased it.\n\nThis also happened with the Valentine's Day bow and arrow. People could not tell if you could actually pull it back in VR or not until getting to see it in person or just buying it and finding out.\n\nThere are plenty more examples but those are the most notable ones off the top of my head.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-03-05T22:33:46.014Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Product descriptions (the one's seen when scrolling underneath a listing to view attached products) typically don't give a lot of information about the functionality of the product and what it offers.\n\nThis is very annoying for viewing items that are limited time, asking to buy it without knowing that information or wait until someone else does to explain it to you.\n\nEspecially for Items, it would be nice to see more thorough descriptions for products on their functionality and what they offer specifically (are there stations? contacts? what are the contact sender tags? random elements? etc).\n\nEmbedded shows a screenshot of a recent example of how unhelpful the product description can be for telling the functionality of an item.",
